# Support email triage

This workflow classifies each incoming support email as an order-status request, a refund request, or other. It looks up order status only for order-status requests. A customer reply is attempted only after the lookup is assessed as reliable; refunds, other emails, uncertain classifications, and unreliable or failed lookups go to the support queue. Refunds are never issued automatically.

## Configure connectors

The tool declarations are operator-configured placeholders. Set the environment values for the inbound connector spec, order-system spec, SMTP credentials and sender/recipient configuration, and support-queue webhook URL before deployment. Do not commit credentials, URLs, or email addresses.

The application must supply `Main` with `incoming_email_text`, `verified_order_reference`, and `customer_reply_destination`. The order reference and reply destination should come from the trusted inbound integration, not from model-generated text. The original email text is sent only to the classifier. The lookup agent receives an order reference and has only the order-system tool; the reply agent receives typed case details and has only the sending tools.

The sending tools require Support reviewer approval. Configure the email connector for the intended per-customer reply behavior before production use; the placeholder SMTP recipient configuration is not a substitute for a verified recipient-routing policy.

If classification or a required action fails, the workflow stops rather than sending an unverified customer reply or issuing a refund. If support routing fails, the case must be left unprocessed and reported for operator intervention.

Run the scripted workflow tests with:

```text
weave test main.loom
```

Review the project without making live calls with:

```text
weave check main.loom --no-env
weave review main.loom
```
