=== file: README.md ===
# Support email triage

This workflow classifies each incoming support email as an order-status request, a refund request, or other. It looks up order status only for order-status requests. A customer reply is attempted only after the lookup is assessed as reliable; refunds, other emails, uncertain classifications, and unreliable or failed lookups go to the support queue. Refunds are never issued automatically.

## Configure connectors

The tool declarations are operator-configured placeholders. Set the environment values for the inbound connector spec, order-system spec, SMTP credentials and sender/recipient configuration, and support-queue webhook URL before deployment. Do not commit credentials, URLs, or email addresses.

The application must supply `Main` with `customer_email_payload`, `trusted_order_key`, `verified_recipient_address`, and `trusted_message_identifier`. The order reference, recipient address, and message identifier must come from the trusted inbound integration, not from model-generated text. The original email text is sent only to the classifier. The lookup agent receives only the trusted order reference and has the read-only order-system tool; the reply agent receives typed case details and has only the sending tools.

For production, configure the order-system OpenAPI spec to expose only read operations and the approved order lookup. Configure the inbound connector to expose only the permitted email fields. The SMTP and support-queue connectors are placeholders and must be configured for their intended destinations.

Refunds and cases requiring fallback are routed to the support queue and presented to the Support reviewer. Refunds are never issued automatically. If a send fails or its outcome is unknown, the workflow does not retry that send. If support routing fails, the case is left unprocessed and reported for operator intervention.

Run the scripted workflow tests with:

```text
weave test main.loom
```

Review the project without making live calls with:

```text
weave check main.loom --no-env
weave review main.loom
```
=== end

